            <ArticleTitle>Delayed massive bleeding two years after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>476-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4293/108680813x13693422518470</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="INTRODUCTION" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Delayed massive bleeding from an ischemic ulcer is a complication after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGB). Ischemic ulcers that present with massive bleeding are rare and challenging for the gastroenterologist as well as the bariatric surgeon.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE DESCRIPTION" NlmCategory="METHODS">This report reviews the case of a 63-year-old man who underwent an uncomplicated laparoscopic RYGB for morbid obesity and experienced two episodes of massive hemorrhage after the procedure, almost 1 year apart.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">To our knowledge, there are only a few such specific cases reported. Here, we describe the treatment and outcome for such a case and present a review of the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
